><td align="char">&#x02212;20</td><td align="char">5.11</td></tr><tr><td/><td/><td/><td/><td/><td align="left">L</td><td align="char">&#x02212;24</td><td align="char">&#x02212;56</td><td align="char">&#x02212;24</td><td align="char">5.12</td></tr><tr><td colspan="11" align="left">&#x02028;&#x02028;</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x000a0;Primary visual cortex (V1)</td><td align="left">L/R</td><td align="char">0</td><td align="char">&#x02212;82</td><td align="char">2</td><td align="char">5.05</td><td align="left">L/R</td><td align="char">0</td><td align="char">&#x02212;92</td><td align="char">6</td><td align="char">5.89</td></tr><tr><td colspan="11" align="left">&#x02028;&#x02028;</td></tr><tr><td colspan="11" align="left">(ii) Decreasing signal with increasing force</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x000a0;None</td><td/><td/><td/><td/><td/><td/><td/><td/><td/><td/></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Voxels in which hand grip-related signal change increases linearly with increasing hand grip force. All voxels are significant at <italic>P</italic>&#x000a0;&#x0003c;&#x000a0;0.05, corrected for multiple comparisons across whole brain.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tbl3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Age-related changes in the main effects of hand grip</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left">Region</th><th colspan="6" align="left">Right hand<hr/></th><th colspan="6" align="left">Left hand<hr/></th></tr><tr><th/><th align="left">Side</th><th colspan="3" align="left">Talairach coordinates in MNI space<hr/></th><th align="left"><italic>Z</italic>-value</th><th align="left">Correlation analysis (<italic>r</italic><sup>2</sup>)</th><th align="left">Side</th><th colspan="3" align="left">Talairach coordinates in MNI space<hr/></th><th align="left"><italic>Z</italic>-value</th><th align="left">Correlation analysis (<italic>r</italic><sup>2</sup>)</th></tr><tr><th/><th/><th align="left"><ita